{
  "title": "Media Profiles: Resize and Crop Images Consistently | Orchard Core",
  "description": "A picture in the Media Library keeps its own size, but a site needs it wide for a banner in one place and small for a thumbnail in another. Writing those sizes out page by page makes them hard to keep the same.\n\nMedia profiles give each size a name. A profile stores image settings such as a width, a height, a resize mode, a format and a quality, and a theme asks for it by name, so one change reaches every page that uses it.\n\nIn this video:\n• Why media profiles exist\n• The Media Profiles page\n• The resize modes: Max, Crop, Pad and Stretch\n• Creating a profile\n• Changing the banner profile and seeing it on the site\n• Searching for and deleting profiles",
